  "answer": "Based on the CDC's National Vital Statistics Report \"Deaths: Final Data for 2022\" (Table 17), four US states had age-adjusted death rates exceeding all three thresholds in 2022:\n\n| State | Heart Disease | Cancer | Diabetes |\n|-------|--------------|--------|----------|\n| **Arkansas** | 224.1 | 168.1 | 36.0 |\n| **Mississippi** | 248.0 | 178.4 | 34.7 |\n| **Oklahoma** | 257.1 | 171.6 | 33.8 |\n| **West Virginia** | 209.5 | 176.3 | 41.1 |\n\n**Thresholds:** Heart disease >191.5, Cancer >161.9, Diabetes >33.1 (all age-adjusted rates per 100,000 U.S. standard population).\n\nSource: CDC/NCHS, National Vital Statistics Reports Volume 74, Number 4 (June 10, 2025), Table 17 — age-adjusted death rates for 2022 by state for Diseases of heart (I00–I09,I11,I13,I20–I51), Malignant neoplasms (C00–C97), and Diabetes mellitus (E10–E14).",
